    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABAK3jGA",
      "title": "pcd: align specs with the shipped deployment pipeline",
      "author": "0xiamflux",
      "number": 930,
      "body": "## Context\r\nThe PCD spec pages landed before super root support and the `prepare` / `prestate` /\r\n`continue` hardening merged. This updates all three against the code that shipped. Spec-only.\r\n\r\n- Both game families are deployable at genesis. New definitions for Super Root, Starting Anchor\r\n  Root, Selected Prestate and Fallback Prestate replace `Prestate / Prestate Hash`, and\r\n  `iOPD-002` pins the root and its `l2SequenceNumber` per family.\r\n- OPCM's game-type check is scoped to the `SUPER_ROOT_GAMES_MIGRATION` mode, plus the three\r\n  value checks PCD added: non-zero anchor root, no `0xdead` placeholder, non-zero prestate.\r\n- `DeployOPChainInput` gains `startingAnchorRoot` and `cannonAbsolutePrestate`. A permissionless\r\n  deploy enables the respected game and its guardian fallback.\r\n- Command behavior now matches the pipeline: anchor pinning, prestate invalidation on every\r\n  `prepare`, and `continue`'s digest, fork-simulation, anchor and post-deploy checks.\r\n- The `BLOCKHASH` and second-RPC guards never shipped and are replaced by what the code does.\r\n\r\nClaims verified against `615b1c75dd` and `9714d4dd2c` on `develop` and op-deployer's three\r\ncommands.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-18T16:09:12Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-02T18:59:28Z",
      "additions": 392,
      "deletions": 133
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABDw2k5w",
      "title": "Refresh the smart contract architecture overview",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 946,
      "body": "The overview still used the older dispute-game contracts and omitted the L2 contract upgrade path. Update the L1 diagrams for U20 with ETHLockbox enabled, and document the Karst L2 upgrade flow.\n\n- Show super-root games, withdrawal validation, ETH custody, and the correct pause and owner permissions.\n- Add the L2ContractsManager upgrade flow and supporting predeploys, OperatorFeeVault, and beacon-root and block-history notes.\n- Separate dense diagrams by purpose, use consistent colors, and move pause and permission details into nearby notes. Correct the ERC721 bridge labels and distinguish fixed implementations from upgradeable proxies.\n\nValidation: Markdown, table-of-contents, spelling and filename checks, book build, and overview links. Reviewed all seven rendered diagrams in light and dark themes.\n\nCircleCI `lint-specs` and `build-book` passed.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-16T12:21:51Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-18T18:44:03Z",
      "additions": 233,
      "deletions": 182
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABAjzvdQ",
      "title": "specs: replace flashblocks with subblocks",
      "author": "bitwiseguy",
      "number": 933,
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Replace the detailed Flashblocks specification with a minimal, consumer-facing Subblocks specification.\n- Document the WebSocket payload format, sequencing guarantees, JSON-RPC behavior, and transaction inclusion implications.\n- Clarify that Subblocks are a backwards-compatible successor to Flashblocks, except that `state_root`, `block_hash`, `withdrawals_root`, and `withdrawals` are zeroed.\n- Update the specs book summary and spelling dictionary.\n\n## Related Issues\n* Closes https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/issues/929",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T14:09:14Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-01T13:41:07Z",
      "additions": 200,
      "deletions": 1398
    }
